==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Hurricat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Catyphoon''' when obtained from [[Revenge of Red Sky (Merciless)|Revenge of Red Sky]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
[[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies beware! Catornado has Area Attack and the second fastest attack rate of all [[Cat Units]], dealing constant [[Critical Hit]]s to groups of enemies. Even when he doesn't land Critical Hits, his godly attack rate can still shred weaker Metals such as [[Metal Hippoe]], [[Metal Doge]], [[Croconator]] and to a certain extent, [[Metal One Horn]]. Overall, Catornado is a great anti-Metal unit, but make sure to support him with other [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critters]] when facing more durable Metals like [[Super Metal Hippoe]], [[Sir Metal Seal]] and [[Metal Cyclone]], as Catornado's damage and range typically won't be enough to deal with them on his own.

While his damage per hit is low, Hurricat has one of the highest DPS of all non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]]/[[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cats]] that can deal Critical Area Attacks. His relatively low Critical rate also means that he benefits significantly from critical hit combos such as [[Miracle Performance (Combo)|Miracle Performance]], effectively raising his expected DPS against Metal enemies by about 40%.

In [[Cats in the Snow]], this unit can act as a shield against the [[Snowball]] as they have very low HP and range and Catornado has a godly attack rate, effectively destroying all incoming Snowballs before getting hit.

==='''True Form'''===
Catyphoon gains improved health and speed. The increased health is helpful, but not a drastic buff, while the speed boost is insignificant and can even be a downside in some cases, such as trying to cheese [[Final Tower]]. Overall, unlike most of the [[:Category:Cyclone Stages|Cyclone Stages]]' drops, this True Form doesn't bring a lot of improvements, but is still worth getting if you're able to complete the stage it drops from.

